# Docker only reads a .dockerignore from the build context root (or a
# Dockerfile-specific one also placed at the context root) - all of this
# project's compose builds use context: ../../.. (the repo root) from
# infra/docker/compose/, so this is the only .dockerignore that is ever
# actually applied. A copy previously lived at infra/docker/.dockerignore
# and was never read by any build; moved here with paths updated for the
# June 2026 structure flatten (backend/ -> src/backend/, frontend/ ->
# src/frontend/).

# VCS
.git
.gitignore

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
src/backend/venv/
src/backend/.pytest_cache/
src/backend/.mypy_cache/
src/backend/.coverage
src/backend/htmlcov/
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Local data, secrets and generated files. None of them is in the repository, all of them can
# be in a working tree, and the Dockerfile copies src/backend whole: an image built from a
# tree that had been used carried its local databases, its generated export files (student
# data), its saved mail settings and a backup key. A pattern here applies at the root of the
# build context only unless it starts with **/ - which is why "__pycache__/" and "*.pyc"
# above never matched anything under src/, and "src/backend/venv/" missed ".venv".
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.keys/
**/local-secrets/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
src/backend/data/
src/backend/exports/
src/backend/imports/
src/backend/logs/
src/backend/backups/
src/backend/test-results/
src/backend/.ruff_cache/

# Node
src/frontend/node_modules/
src/frontend/.vite/
src/frontend/dist/
src/frontend/.eslintcache

# Builds & artifacts
build/
dist/
coverage/
.backups/
backups/
logs/
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker
**/.dockerignore
**/Dockerfile*
